WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
(melodic piano music)

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.140
- [Wall Street] We gonna
go ahead and get situated.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:07.060
This is the finance program, and we always

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.763
like to see new faces.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.850
- [Rahsaan] When you come to Wall Street's

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.220
financial literacy class,
you're gonna see people

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.250
with tattoos and dreds,
and just people you

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.850
normally wouldn't expect
to see learning finance.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.930
You're gonna see people with
all different backgrounds

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.350
looking for hope.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.632
He makes it universal.

00:00:23.632 --> 00:00:26.799
(melodic piano music)

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.200
- If I tell you I'll
give you the 50 bucks,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.170
but I want you to pay
me back $50 in interest,

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.120
what you gonna say?

00:00:37.176 --> 00:00:38.009
- I'm gonna say "no."

00:00:38.009 --> 00:00:38.842
- You gonna say what?

00:00:38.842 --> 00:00:40.440
- No.
- And why you gonna say no?

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.610
- They call me Wall Street because I teach

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.430
all of the financial
classes here at San Quentin.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:48.220
I've been teaching financial education

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.563
for about 10 years now.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:54.680
I am in prison for participating
in a robbery-murder,

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.200
and I was sentenced to 54
years to life in prison

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.423
for that crime, and I've been
incarcerated now for 22 years.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:06.140
These are the stocks that I picked,

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.770
MasterCard, I got at 89, they're at 200.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.950
- Wall Street came to prison illiterate.

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:14.430
He doesn't have a college
education to this day;

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:17.450
he only has a GED, and yet,
this guy is successfully

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.960
trading from prison.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.580
- Marcelli, who had come
from juvenile hall with me,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.120
he would read the sports
page to me, he'd be like,

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.140
man, go get it; and I'll read
it, and I grabbed the paper,

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.360
and I was like, I got it.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.050
When I turned around, an
older guy said, "Hey, man

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:30.470
"you play the stock market?"

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.720
And I realized that I picked
up the business section

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:33.670
instead of the sports page.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.040
I was like, ah, man, and I asked him

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.970
what the stock market was,
and he told me, he said,

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.590
that's the place where white
folks keep all their money.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.650
And that's when I really first
discovered the stock market.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.050
So, I started teaching myself how to read.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:49.180
Family or friends on the outside opened up

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.890
online brokerage accounts,
and I basically told them

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.400
what to buy and when to
buy and when to sell.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.313
And it was just simply, it
was really just that easy.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.593
This is the finance program,

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:05.430
but I don't teach about finance.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:10.430
I teach financial empowerment
emotional literacy.

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:12.183
That's what I teach.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.930
So, I think financial
education is important

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.150
for incarcerated people,
given that the crimes

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:22.260
that are committed are
financially motivated and driven.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.450
When I learned about
financial education myself,

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.640
I thought that would be
something that other men

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.640
in my same situation could benefit from.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.170
And so now the program
teaches incarcerated men

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:38.110
how to better manage their
emotions and relations

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.770
to their financial standing.

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.210
So, you gotta weigh your strategies

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.860
when you're talking about
giving yourself room

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:44.960
to start saving money.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.430
- When you're traumatized
you do a lot of things

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.040
you don't know why you're doing them.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.470
And that happens with finance, too.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:53.960
I suffered a lot of trauma in my life,

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:57.773
and my trauma culminated
in me murdering a man.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.980
So, while this is very important
to me because I do need

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.350
to manage my money and manage my life,

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.860
what's most important is that I'm managing

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.840
my emotional responsibilities,
because the last time

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.743
I didn't do that, a man lost his life.

00:03:14.589 --> 00:03:16.280
- I don't think you can
have full rehabilitation

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.690
without financial education.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.870
I can make amends for the
crimes that I've done,

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.280
I can even stop doing the
things that I've done,

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:26.970
but I think for people who were criminals,

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.820
when you empower those
people, and they know

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.030
that they don't have to
commit a crime like I did,

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.580
when I learned I didn't
have to commit crime,

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.250
it was like, wow, I can really
make something of my life

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.731
and not have to be a criminal.

00:03:36.731 --> 00:03:39.898
(melodic piano music)

